Architect: your correction is right. My earlier "owner decided to pay" was wrong; §9.5 as you wrote it is correct. Four small calls:

1. Don't wait for the payment decision to start R0. With the owner's clicks, the current free-tier export gets the free Rig Check plus auto-rig (25 of the 200 free credits). That answers the feasibility question about the route now. Label the results "free-tier mesh". If R0 passes on it, re-run on a Pro mesh only if the owner later pays. If it fails, first check whether the failure comes from mesh quality (fused limbs, noise) or from the route (coat, Humanoid mapping). Only a mesh-quality failure argues for paying.
2. If the owner pays, monthly only, never annual. The owner can turn off auto-renew right after subscribing, so cancellation pain doesn't matter.
3. API top-up: not needed for R0. It only matters at G5 batch (automation). Don't price it or ask for it until then.
4. S2 normal-map check fails (9.5% > 2%): record it, don't fix it. G0 is judged on appearance only, so no detail work. The same rule applies to S1 and S3.

The escalation triggers you listed match the plan. Go.
